course: dictionary
lesson: 4350
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words and sentences around it, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «Chloe's guinea pigs squeak like a car alarm every morning when she comes downstairs.» Squeaking and coming downstairs tell you guinea pigs are animals here.
explain: «Be my guinea pig for this recipe.» There is no animal in this sentence. A guinea pig here is a person who tries something new first. The word recipe is your clue, because you test a recipe before anyone else eats it.
explain: Capital letters are clues too. Guinea with a capital G is a place, such as Guinea in West Africa or New Guinea, a big island north of Australia. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then try it in the sentence to check.
fact: A guinea pig is a small, furry pet rodent with no tail.
fact: Guinea pigs are rodents, not pigs, and they do not come from Guinea.
fact: A guinea pig can also be a person who tries something out first.
fact: A guinea was an old British gold coin, worth a little more than a pound.
fact: Guinea (capital G) is a country in West Africa, and New Guinea is a big island north of Australia.
exercise: «Chloe's guinea pigs squeak like a car alarm every morning.» What is a guinea pig in this sentence? | A big island near Australia | A coin worth a pound | A country in West Africa | *A small furry pet with no tail
exercise: «Be my guinea pig for this recipe.» Which meaning fits best? | A small pet with no tail | A place in West Africa | *Someone who tries something new first | An old gold coin
exercise: Which word means an old British gold coin? | Guinea pig | Guinea fowl | New Guinea | *A guinea
test: Are guinea pigs pigs? | Yes, they are a kind of fish | Yes, they are a kind of pig | *No, they are rodents | Yes, they come from Guinea
test: In «a frog from Papua New Guinea», what does Guinea with a capital G name? | An animal | A coin | A kind of pet | *A place, a country
exam: Which meaning fits best when a teacher says, «Each of you will be a guinea pig for our new science test»? | A country in West Africa | A small furry pet rodent | *A person who tries something new first | A gold coin worth a pound
